// CONVERGE acceptance item 4 (operator directive C, 2026-08-09): the host-key
// fingerprint ENROLLMENT registry. The executed reach probe landed every fleet host at
// ProbeHostKeyUnenrolled — the transport refuses verification because the probing
// account holds no known_hosts entry, so first-contact and changed-key are
// indistinguishable and both P0 cells honestly read Inaccessible. This module is the
// remedy the fold names: (a) a wet SCAN observes each host's public key from the same
// LAN position every probe runs from (ssh-keyscan + ssh-keygen -lf, captured to a typed
// receipt — an OBSERVATION, it repairs nothing, per the observe-never-silently-repair
// ordering law); (b) the committed registry rows below are the single enrollment
// authority (the Spark rows cross-check against bold-eagle-107's independent
// measurement of distinct keys); (c) a separate wet ENROLL applies the registry to the
// probing account's known_hosts with an independent ssh-keygen -F readback per host.
// Once enrolled, a verification failure at probe time is a REAL ProbeHostKeyMismatch
// (enrolled expectation contradicted) rather than Unenrolled — the constructor split's
// second arm becomes reachable with a Present expectation.
//
// HostKeyEnrollmentProvenance names WHAT GROUNDS an enrolled host key, because a
// fingerprint row is only as trustworthy as the fact behind it (host-key audit,
// witty-raven-412 / bold-eagle-107 cross-check, 2026-08-10). Two arms, a genuine
// fleet-wide distinction rather than one lane's state:
//   - ScannedFirstContact: the key was captured by ssh-keyscan from the very address the
//     probe is about to trust — trust-on-first-use, grounded in NOTHING but first
//     contact. This is the measured, honest state for srv1..srv4: no cited router
//     reservation, no procurement/serial record, no external key authority exists for
//     those hosts (checked in fleet_physical_inventory and fleet_intent_network before
//     concluding). scanned_from records the address+method so the TOFU is visible.
//   - IndependentlyAnchored: the enrollment is corroborated by an externally-authored
//     fact tying the address to a known unit (a cited CR1000A MAC reservation, ARP-
//     confirmed, authored independently of anything the host says) — an identity join,
//     not trust-on-first-use. authority is REQUIRED and NonEmptyStr, so a row cannot
//     claim this arm without naming a non-empty authority: the "anchored but unnamed"
//     state has no constructor (construction over validation, §5 — no witness restates
//     what the carrier already forbids). The srv5/srv6 DGX Spark units are the intended
//     inhabitant (gunbc.spark.dgx_procurement carries their cited CR1000A reservations,
//     and the slot->box assignment IS decided — dgx_spark_router_binding_operator_allocation,
//     SPARK-ALLOC-LAND-0 2026-08-07, ascending address order as it then stood; the units
//     moved to their wireless interfaces on 2026-08-27 and the addresses are now
//     srv5->192.168.1.226, srv6->192.168.1.225 — the join is to a box, not a number, so the
//     allocation is unaffected). They stay ScannedFirstContact here NOT because the binding is
//     open (it is not) but because the anchored-enrollment JOIN has not been PERFORMED: no
//     one has yet enrolled a Spark host key, observed the MAC at that address, and matched
//     it against the cited reservation row. IndependentlyAnchored would be a claim about
//     work that has not happened — the same over-claim in a different place. The anchor is
//     AVAILABLE but UNUSED; the arm is ready for bold-eagle to flip these two once that
//     join executes, with no widening edit.
type HostKeyEnrollmentProvenance
  = ScannedFirstContact { scanned_from: NonEmptyStr }
  | IndependentlyAnchored { authority: NonEmptyStr }

type KnownHostKeyRow {
  host: HostIdentity
  endpoint: String
  key_type: String
  public_key_base64: String
  sha256_fingerprint: String
  provenance: HostKeyEnrollmentProvenance
}

// 🟡 dissolve-on: like the probe-receipt ledger, rows land here as the provenance-backed
// transcription of an executed scan receipt; DISSOLVES WHEN scan-artifact ingestion
// commits rows by machinery (same trigger as probe_receipt_ledger_transcription_scaffold).
data host_key_enrollment_transcription_scaffold: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.fleet_host_key_enrollment",
    decl_name: "fleet_host_key_enrollments",
    field: WholeDeclaration,
  }
}

